- No, but I took the morning-after pill!
- 90% safe. 10% is the catch.

243
00:22:02.466 --> 00:22:04.967
There's a loo here
if you want to use it.

244
00:22:09.239 --> 00:22:11.442
Fuck, fuck, fuck!

245
00:22:22.419 --> 00:22:24.353
Bollocks.

246
00:22:26.809 --> 00:22:29.422
<i>Alex, are you there? Can we meet?</i>

247
00:22:37.267 --> 00:22:40.772
<i>I'd love to, but Bethany's parents
are taking us out to dinner at the Hazel.</i>

248
00:22:40.972 --> 00:22:43.539
<i>How posh is that?</i>

249
00:24:10.294 --> 00:24:12.120
Okay. I'm sorry.

250
00:24:12.463 --> 00:24:14.198
I... I...

251
00:24:14.897 --> 00:24:16.600
I've got news.

252
00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:19.557
- Me, too.
- Read it.

253
00:24:28.245 --> 00:24:30.605
Scholarship to Harvard!

254
00:24:32.049 --> 00:24:35.253
Alex, that's so great. Congratulations.

255
00:24:35.353 --> 00:24:38.257
It's unbelievable, right?

256
00:24:38.657 --> 00:24:40.885
Have you heard back
from Boston College, yet?

257
00:24:42.452 --> 00:24:43.592
No.

258
00:24:45.797 --> 00:24:48.667
- Yeah, you'll get in.
- What about Bethany? Have you told her?

259
00:24:49.155 --> 00:24:51.102
She'll be fine.

260
00:24:51.202 --> 00:24:54.539
She's got this... Oh, God,
she's got this thing about my hair.

261
00:24:54.639 --> 00:24:56.308
- Yeah.
- But she literally yanks it.

262
00:24:56.408 --> 00:24:58.774
And she pulls this funny face
during sex like this...

263
00:24:59.310 --> 00:25:01.777
- I think she likes it.
- Enough. Enough.

264
00:25:03.314 --> 00:25:06.117
Don't you care what she's gonna
think about you rushing off like this?

265
00:25:06.563 --> 00:25:09.087
- All right, what is it?
- What?

266
00:25:09.187 --> 00:25:11.468
Well, you're defending Bethany.
What's wrong?

267
00:25:11.568 --> 00:25:13.122
Nothing. Nothing's wrong.

268
00:25:15.626 --> 00:25:17.599
I thought you'd be happier.

269
00:25:17.699 --> 00:25:21.132
We're on our way to Boston!
Come on! Hey?

270
00:25:21.232 --> 00:25:23.034
It's great. It's great, really.

271
00:25:24.467 --> 00:25:27.488
- Well done.
- What, come on, you're coming, too!

272
00:25:27.588 --> 00:25:33.006
My flight's in three days, which gives me
time to get settled in before term starts.

273
00:25:33.506 --> 00:25:35.364
You need to go ahead
and book your ticket.

274
00:25:35.464 --> 00:25:37.079
Sure.

275
00:25:37.181 --> 00:25:41.912
I... have got some stuff
to sort first, but...

276
00:25:42.507 --> 00:25:44.216
I'll be there.

277
00:25:48.259 --> 00:25:50.462
- Don't get blown up by terrorists.
- Okay.

278
00:25:50.562 --> 00:25:52.431
Or lose cabin pressure
and fall out of the sky.

279
00:25:52.531 --> 00:25:54.866
- Rosie, wait, wait, wait...
- Or fly into a flock of birds. I mean it!

280
00:25:54.966 --> 00:25:57.068
I can delay, if you need me to.

281
00:25:59.169 --> 00:26:01.737
No. You're getting on that plane.

282
00:26:03.273 --> 00:26:04.759
I've got you something.

283
00:26:04.859 --> 00:26:07.944
Close your eyes. Close your eyes.

284
00:26:09.146 --> 00:26:12.814
Give me your finger.
Okay. Keep it there.

285
00:26:21.037 --> 00:26:22.434
North America.

286
00:27:14.211 --> 00:27:16.278
Keep in touch, okay?

287
00:27:18.801 --> 00:27:20.182
Okay.

288
00:27:22.552 --> 00:27:25.403
See you in two weeks, so...

289
00:27:32.362 --> 00:27:33.993
Boston.

290
00:27:36.563 --> 00:27:37.500
This way?

291
00:28:03.994 --> 00:28:06.831
If I'd told him, he'd never have left and his
whole life would have been ruined, too.

292
00:28:06.931 --> 00:28:08.366
I mean, what's the point?

293
00:28:08.466 --> 00:28:11.069
How noble. I'd have forced
the bastard to stay.

294
00:28:11.169 --> 00:28:15.139
Oh, no, no. He's not the dad.
That's just some other loser.

295
00:28:15.811 --> 00:28:18.877
You are turning out to be
a lot more interesting than you look.

296
00:28:18.977 --> 00:28:22.736
- Why don't you just get rid of the thing?
- My parents are Catholic.

297
00:28:22.836 --> 00:28:26.481
I don't believe in all that,
but I can't!

298
00:28:26.850 --> 00:28:29.220
Oh, I had it all sussed!

299
00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:33.925
Move to Boston, study, get a great job,
at 27, come back and open a hotel.

300
00:28:34.025 --> 00:28:37.495
- Then get married and have kids.
- Wow. A whole life in bullet points.

301
00:28:37.595 --> 00:28:40.932
Yeah, well now, it's pregnant,
have sprog, full-time mother,

302
00:28:41.032 --> 00:28:44.669
wave goodbye to career,
live off benefits, grow fat, lose hair.

303
00:28:44.769 --> 00:28:49.436
Yeah. You might as well just kill
yourself now. I can sort the drugs.

304
00:28:50.574 --> 00:28:51.747
Look.

305
00:28:51.847 --> 00:28:56.312
There's loads of people out there that want
a kid that can't have one. Give it away.

306
00:28:58.648 --> 00:29:01.149
I could still move to Boston.

307
00:29:01.920 --> 00:29:05.123
I can apply to college again,
or get a job. I don't care.

308
00:29:05.223 --> 00:29:07.459
So it would all be the same,
just six months later. I mean,

309
00:29:07.559 --> 00:29:09.995
I don't even need to tell Alex,
I could just think of an excuse.

310
00:29:10.095 --> 00:29:12.729
Whoa. That's major denial, babe.

311
00:29:12.931 --> 00:29:14.432
Yeah.

312
00:29:14.532 --> 00:29:17.365
I just happen to think
it's the way to go.

313
00:29:26.845 --> 00:29:28.713
- Who's that?
- Alex.

314
00:29:28.813 --> 00:29:30.048
Have you told him yet?

315
00:29:30.148 --> 00:29:33.284
I'm sending him my arrival time in Boston.
That's all he needs to know.

316
00:29:33.384 --> 00:29:36.318
All this fibbing is gonna
catch up with you, girl.

317
00:29:38.923 --> 00:29:41.390
The way that thing burst out of her.

318
00:29:41.859 --> 00:29:43.867
- That might happen to you!
- It might.

319
00:29:44.694 --> 00:29:47.766
Her whole belly will erupt.
Blood and guts.

320
00:29:47.866 --> 00:29:51.136
And this freakish alien will
leap out and bite your head off!

321
00:29:51.636 --> 00:29:54.873
Stop it, the pair of you!
Pregnancy is a sacred thing!

322
00:29:55.073 --> 00:29:57.041
- It can't hear us.
- Yes, it can!

323
00:29:57.141 --> 00:30:00.411
- And don't refer to it as "it."
- It's a girl if you must know.

324
00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:02.400
You found out?

325
00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:04.383
I asked at the last scan.

326
00:30:04.483 --> 00:30:07.049
I thought I should tell the social worker
so he can start his plans.

327
00:30:07.651 --> 00:30:09.607
A girl!

328
00:30:10.221 --> 00:30:14.556
- What about names?
- No, I'll let the new parents decide.

329
00:30:15.358 --> 00:30:16.662
- Give us a peek.
- Hey!

330
00:30:16.823 --> 00:30:20.498
A woman's body doesn't become public property
just because she is pregnant, you know.

331
00:30:20.598 --> 00:30:21.730
Be my guest.

332
00:30:26.970 --> 00:30:29.187
Look at that!

333
00:30:30.107 --> 00:30:33.084
Oh, my God!

334
00:30:34.211 --> 00:30:36.281
She's got hiccups!

335
00:30:36.670 --> 00:30:38.213
The little thing's got hiccups!

336
00:30:38.949 --> 00:30:41.339
Oh, bless!

337
00:30:42.719 --> 00:30:44.525
Whatever.

338
00:30:56.433 --> 00:30:58.900
Baby, can you hear me?

339
00:31:03.841 --> 00:31:07.975
Try holding your breath like this.

340
00:31:15.919 --> 00:31:18.553
There you are, Katie girl!

341
00:31:22.659 --> 00:31:27.128
That's probably not going to
be your name, okay?

342
00:31:33.670 --> 00:31:36.574
It's coming! Towels! Hot water!

343
00:31:36.674 --> 00:31:39.241
- Where's the midwife?
- I don't know!

344
00:31:40.463 --> 00:31:42.878
Come in now! Come on!

345
00:31:43.246 --> 00:31:44.883
- Come on!
- Midwife's here!

346
00:31:44.983 --> 00:31:48.850
Let's go! As quick as you like!
She's just right down the hallway.

347
00:31:49.621 --> 00:31:52.754
- All right, okay, breathe, breathe!
- Get out!

348
00:31:53.859 --> 00:31:56.527
Breathe, everything is
going to be all right!

349
00:31:56.627 --> 00:31:59.127
- Being a girl sucks!
- Yeah.

350
00:32:03.201 --> 00:32:05.325
Hello.

351
00:32:07.671 --> 00:32:09.905
That'll be the social worker.

352
00:32:11.975 --> 00:32:14.223
Would you like to hold her?

353
00:32:14.579 --> 00:32:17.252
Or should I bring her
straight downstairs?

354
00:32:48.511 --> 00:32:50.345
Katie.

355
00:32:52.349 --> 00:32:55.013
Sweet little Katie.

356
00:33:22.179 --> 00:33:24.702
I promise, Katie,

357
00:33:25.483 --> 00:33:28.049
I'm going to be a good Mommy.

358
00:33:44.156 --> 00:33:45.893
Katie.

359
00:33:46.203 --> 00:33:48.014
Katie.

360
00:33:58.014 --> 00:34:00.382
It's gonna be okay.

361
00:34:02.185 --> 00:34:06.330
Please. Katie, it's gonna be okay!

362
00:34:10.994 --> 00:34:15.030
- My life's over, Dad!
- Wait 'til you become a grandparent.

363
00:34:17.034 --> 00:34:19.901
Katie, Katie.

364
00:34:26.610 --> 00:34:30.949
You know, I still remember the drive back
from the hospital when you were born.

365
00:34:31.049 --> 00:34:35.241
You screamed blue murder,
the whole bloody journey.

366
00:34:36.319 --> 00:34:38.723
I was so scared,
I jumped three red lights.

367
00:34:38.823 --> 00:34:41.357
- Lost my license.
- You never told me that before.

368
00:34:43.126 --> 00:34:44.359
You weren't part of the club.

369
00:34:55.272 --> 00:34:58.777
<i>In battle to preserve sanity,
must remember following rules.</i>

370
00:34:58.877 --> 00:35:02.344
<i>Number one, never breast feed
in a public place.</i>

371
00:35:04.112 --> 00:35:07.983
<i>Two, never bounce Katie
on knee after feeding.</i>

372
00:35:10.020 --> 00:35:13.220
<i>Three, try not to cry when she cries.</i>

373
00:35:13.857 --> 00:35:16.161
<i>And four, the most important of all,</i>

374
00:35:16.261 --> 00:35:19.327
<i>never assume trouble
isn't around the next corner.</i>

375
00:35:19.596 --> 00:35:22.409
- Laters, girls.
- Bye.

376
00:35:42.852 --> 00:35:44.695
Rosie? Oh, no.

377
00:35:44.895 --> 00:35:48.356
Tragic. Are you okay?

378
00:35:50.161 --> 00:35:53.762
- Tell me that's not yours!
- No!

379
00:35:55.098 --> 00:35:56.735
What, you're a nanny now?

380
00:35:56.935 --> 00:35:59.712
Yeah! You know,
at least it's good money.

381
00:36:00.438 --> 00:36:02.337
I thought you were
going to Boston with Alex.

382
00:36:03.206 --> 00:36:07.311
Oh, no, no, no, I realized children
are the only education you need.

383
00:36:08.304 --> 00:36:10.212
So, who's the dad?

384
00:36:13.684 --> 00:36:15.317
Get it off! Get it off!

385
00:36:17.154 --> 00:36:20.088
- I've got to go!
- Bye, then!

386
00:36:38.775 --> 00:36:40.638
Alex.

387
00:36:41.511 --> 00:36:42.847
What are you doing here?

388
00:36:43.047 --> 00:36:45.617
Just back for the weekend.
Thought I'd surprise you.

389
00:36:45.917 --> 00:36:49.320
Great! Yeah. Let's go for a coffee then.

390
00:36:49.420 --> 00:36:52.754
No, no. Let's stay here.
Why don't you put the kettle on?

391
00:37:01.899 --> 00:37:05.069
- So, what have you been up to?
- Oh, just this and that, you know?

392
00:37:05.169 --> 00:37:07.939
- Nice haircut by the way.
- Yeah, thanks.

393
00:37:08.039 --> 00:37:11.306
- You okay? You seem stressed.
- No! No!

394
00:37:11.941 --> 00:37:13.843
So, how's medicine?

395
00:37:13.943 --> 00:37:16.110
Fascinating. Yeah.

396
00:37:16.780 --> 00:37:18.482
We've just been
doing obstetrics, in fact.

397
00:37:18.582 --> 00:37:20.239
Really?

398
00:37:21.484 --> 00:37:24.488
So much to learn. How do you find
these breast pumps, by the way?

399
00:37:24.588 --> 00:37:27.955
- Some women don't like them.
- Oh, total nightmare.

400
00:37:30.159 --> 00:37:31.828
Oh, God.

401
00:37:32.228 --> 00:37:33.678
How did you...

402
00:37:33.778 --> 00:37:35.263
Bethany.

403
00:37:36.766 --> 00:37:38.500
Fast work.

404
00:37:42.605 --> 00:37:45.015
I was gonna tell you, Alex, I promise.

405
00:37:45.115 --> 00:37:46.665
When?

406
00:37:47.544 --> 00:37:50.945
I didn't want to hold you back.

407
00:37:54.417 --> 00:37:56.954
She's had colic for months.

408
00:37:57.054 --> 00:38:00.989
My whole life is feeding,
winding and nappies.

409
00:38:02.259 --> 00:38:04.607
All I can think about is poo.

410
00:38:05.061 --> 00:38:07.229
How much, when, what color.

411
00:38:08.465 --> 00:38:09.731
I hope you mean hers.

412
00:38:16.939 --> 00:38:19.006
What happened to Greg?

413
00:38:19.109 --> 00:38:23.178
He miraculously got a job
in Ibiza the minute he heard.

414
00:38:33.289 --> 00:38:34.939
Can I be godfather?

415
00:38:39.162 --> 00:38:41.529
I'd love nothing more.

416
00:38:55.278 --> 00:38:58.546
I think not telling you

417
00:38:58.648 --> 00:39:01.016
was a way to keep
the dream alive, you know?

418
00:39:03.386 --> 00:39:08.323
So there was at least someone
out there who still saw me as Rosie.

419
00:39:09.659 --> 00:39:14.562
And not this strange,
new person I've become.

420
00:40:26.403 --> 00:40:28.347
So...

421
00:40:28.447 --> 00:40:32.641
the last time I looked that depressed,
I tried to hang myself with my favorite tie.

422
00:40:36.245 --> 00:40:38.680
Hi, I'm Phil.

423
00:40:40.083 --> 00:40:41.321
Alex.

424
00:40:41.421 --> 00:40:44.316
I've been sent to play fairy godmother.

425
00:40:45.388 --> 00:40:47.122
You don't look the part, mate.

426
00:40:48.291 --> 00:40:52.460
My sister's been driving me crazy.
She wants to know, would you buy her a drink?

427
00:40:54.163 --> 00:40:55.953
Which one is she?

428
00:41:01.404 --> 00:41:03.282
The hot girl from class?

429
00:41:03.382 --> 00:41:07.742
Sally. The bright sunflower
in the family window box.

430
00:41:09.879 --> 00:41:12.050
- Hey!
- Hey!

431
00:41:12.150 --> 00:41:15.917
Everybody has been wondering
why the cute British guy looks so sad.

432
00:41:17.386 --> 00:41:18.973
Sorry.

433
00:41:19.589 --> 00:41:22.526
It's time to realize
you're here with us.

434
00:41:22.626 --> 00:41:25.760
And that we might be fun to be with.

435
00:41:31.034 --> 00:41:33.270
Katie! It's your first Christmas!

436
00:41:33.770 --> 00:41:35.206
I hope you got my present!

437
00:41:35.406 --> 00:41:37.775
<i>Thanks for the book, Alex.
I know she'll love it...</i>

438
00:41:38.175 --> 00:41:39.310
- <i>...one day.</i>
- What is it?

439
00:41:39.410 --> 00:41:42.076
This is my new apartment.

440
00:41:42.579 --> 00:41:44.281
What's this you're doing here, darling?

441
00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:46.317
Handmade hearts.

442
00:41:46.417 --> 00:41:49.119
And here, we have my favorite
<i>Back to the Future</i> poster.

443
00:41:49.219 --> 00:41:51.722
It would look so special
in the bathroom.

444
00:41:51.922 --> 00:41:53.188
Walk to Mommy.

445
00:41:53.456 --> 00:41:55.626
- Come to me.
- Good girl!

446
00:41:55.726 --> 00:41:58.960
Katie, darling,
it's your fourth Christmas.

447
00:42:00.997 --> 00:42:03.164
<i>Did, Mommy get my Christmas card?</i>

448
00:42:08.437 --> 00:42:09.473
Really?

449
00:42:09.573 --> 00:42:14.511
<i>Thanks for Katie's present. She wants me
to tell you she can cycle and count to five.</i>

450
00:42:14.611 --> 00:42:18.078
...three, four, five!

451
00:42:18.448 --> 00:42:22.520
<i>Me, I've got a job and finally
moved out of Mom and Dad's.</i>

452
00:42:22.620 --> 00:42:25.323
Miss Dunne! Welcome back to the hotel!

453
00:42:25.423 --> 00:42:27.525
I believe it's the
penthouse suite for you?

454
00:42:27.625 --> 00:42:29.757
That's right, thanks.

455
00:43:15.137 --> 00:43:18.005
Mommy, Mommy!
It's the first day of school!

456
00:43:21.611 --> 00:43:24.348
I heard some beds

457
00:43:24.448 --> 00:43:26.784
were being stolen recently.

458
00:43:26.884 --> 00:43:29.387
- Isn't that strange?
- Yes, Mommy.

459
00:43:29.487 --> 00:43:32.620
This way, no one can
come in and steal ours.

460
00:43:35.524 --> 00:43:37.058
Are you my daddy?

461
00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:41.796
No! No, he's just a nice man that's
helping Mommy out a bit, that's all.

462
00:43:46.036 --> 00:43:47.071
- Damn!
- What?

463
00:43:47.171 --> 00:43:49.103
It's the wrong key!

464
00:44:00.751 --> 00:44:02.317
- My head!
- Come on, whinger!

465
00:44:05.354 --> 00:44:06.990
Over there! Over there!

466
00:44:07.090 --> 00:44:09.626
- Come on, keep going.
- Quick, quick, Mommy!

467
00:44:09.826 --> 00:44:11.459
Excuse me.

468
00:44:14.363 --> 00:44:17.235
- Love you.
- Love you, too.

469
00:44:23.272 --> 00:44:25.443
You dreamt you were an inanimate object?

470
00:44:25.543 --> 00:44:29.947
Yeah, I mean, come on. An arrow flying
through the air! That's pretty cool.

471
00:44:30.347 --> 00:44:33.584
I don't understand.
How can you be a thing?

472
00:44:33.684 --> 00:44:36.387
I don't know.
I've always had dreams like that.

473
00:44:37.287 --> 00:44:39.721
It sounds to me like
self-esteem issues, sweetie.

474
00:44:40.256 --> 00:44:41.870
You may need to talk to someone.

475
00:44:45.128 --> 00:44:49.032
You know, there are razor hairs
in the bathroom, again today.

476
00:44:49.132 --> 00:44:52.503
- Really?
- You know it gives me allergies.

477
00:44:52.803 --> 00:44:55.205
Next time you have
one of your weird dreams,

478
00:44:55.305 --> 00:45:01.208
maybe you should dream you're
something useful like a vacuum cleaner.

479
00:45:01.811 --> 00:45:05.049
- We have a cleaning lady.
- What do you want?

480
00:45:05.149 --> 00:45:07.782
For her to think
we're a pair of fuck-ups?

481
00:45:08.117 --> 00:45:10.219
That's exactly what we are.

482
00:45:24.634 --> 00:45:27.283
- You okay?
- I've got sand in my eyes.

483
00:45:28.271 --> 00:45:30.405
Look at Mommy!

484
00:45:38.715 --> 00:45:40.782
<i>I dreamt I was an arrow.</i>

485
00:45:41.382 --> 00:45:45.431
<i>The little metal bit right at the tip of
an arrow, whizzing through the air.</i>

486
00:46:10.479 --> 00:46:12.658
What have you told the poor brat?
Are you coming home for dad?

487
00:46:12.758 --> 00:46:15.886
No! Just that he sent me a ticket.
I've got no expectations.

488
00:46:15.986 --> 00:46:17.888
Well, good,
because he's got a girlfriend.

489
00:46:17.988 --> 00:46:20.491
Although you know it's funny,
her name didn't come up once.

490
00:46:20.591 --> 00:46:24.394
Yeah, well, Katie's mature enough to know
that when it comes to men, it doesn't matter.

491
00:46:24.494 --> 00:46:26.731
Yeah, well, Katie also knows
that something must have triggered

492
00:46:26.831 --> 00:46:29.115
his sudden enthusiasm to see
her mom, who, by the way,

493
00:46:29.215 --> 00:46:32.634
knows him better than anyone,
and is clearly the best person to judge!

494
00:46:33.469 --> 00:46:35.102
Oh, and...

495
00:46:57.853 --> 00:47:00.962
All right! Good to see you!

496
00:47:02.364 --> 00:47:06.656
- So, tired? Hungry?
- No. Why?

497
00:47:23.419 --> 00:47:25.252
Come on.

498
00:47:27.323 --> 00:47:29.002
Do you want another?

499
00:47:29.725 --> 00:47:32.359
- Yeah.
- All right. I'll be back, okay?

500
00:47:35.056 --> 00:47:37.751
So, you're new here.

501
00:47:38.376 --> 00:47:41.138
- I'm Jonathan.
- Rosie.

502
00:47:41.238 --> 00:47:44.173
Rosie? So what do you do, Rosie?

503
00:47:44.573 --> 00:47:45.743
I'm a mom!

504
00:47:46.043 --> 00:47:50.845
Is that some kind of, performance thing?
You're a drama major?

505
00:47:51.714 --> 00:47:54.715
I'm a mother of a 5-year-old girl!

506
00:47:55.584 --> 00:47:58.052
Cool! Cool!

507
00:47:59.656 --> 00:48:04.325
Can I get you a drink or something?

508
00:48:06.429 --> 00:48:08.195
A gin and tonic.

509
00:48:09.265 --> 00:48:11.435
- Cell? Car keys?
- Oh, dude. Come on.

510
00:48:11.535 --> 00:48:14.117
- Guys, guys, guys, no, no, no!
- It's happening.

511
00:48:14.218 --> 00:48:15.939
- It's gonna happen!
- Come on, come on! Come on! Please!

512
00:48:16.039 --> 00:48:19.040
- One, two, three!
- Okay, okay! Rosie, Rosie, come on...

513
00:48:27.821 --> 00:48:31.152
- Give me a hand.
- All right.

514
00:48:34.824 --> 00:48:37.091
Come on. Come on! I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

515
00:48:40.164 --> 00:48:42.130
You're looking way too hot
right now, Rosie.

516
00:48:48.571 --> 00:48:51.740
Come on, all right, okay.
If you want it like that.

517
00:48:51.840 --> 00:48:53.508
No, no, no!

518
00:49:01.385 --> 00:49:02.984
Bananas?

519
00:49:07.690 --> 00:49:09.557
- Any good?
- No, it's sort of...

520
00:49:12.928 --> 00:49:14.429
Catch.

521
00:49:15.831 --> 00:49:17.364
All right.

522
00:49:18.935 --> 00:49:21.976
"You will live a long and happy life."

523
00:49:22.076 --> 00:49:23.371
- Sweet.
- Oh, can I switch?

524
00:49:24.407 --> 00:49:26.110
- 'Cause you prefer mine?
- I prefer it.

525
00:49:26.410 --> 00:49:30.244
I do, I do. I don't know
what I'm talking about.

526
00:49:30.913 --> 00:49:33.948
Well, you do go here, so you probably
should know what you're talking about.

527
00:49:40.723 --> 00:49:44.258
<i>Strange to think that I could have
lived here and been part of it.</i>

528
00:49:45.428 --> 00:49:48.796
But I don't regret Katie, you know?

529
00:49:49.531 --> 00:49:52.285
I mean, how could I?

530
00:49:52.635 --> 00:49:56.611
She's... she's the most amazing kid.

531
00:50:01.777 --> 00:50:04.311
The weird thing is that...

532
00:50:05.982 --> 00:50:09.116
she reminds me more of you than Greg.

533
00:50:10.352 --> 00:50:13.053
That's probably just 'cause I love her.

534
00:50:29.404 --> 00:50:30.538
We should go.

535
00:50:32.574 --> 00:50:34.426
Yeah.

536
00:50:35.378 --> 00:50:37.014
Seriously cute.

537
00:50:37.114 --> 00:50:39.316
It was a ball of fluff.

538
00:50:39.824 --> 00:50:42.087
No seriously.

539
00:50:44.353 --> 00:50:48.190
Sally. Rosie. Rosie, Sally.

540
00:50:48.290 --> 00:50:50.159
Good morning.

541
00:50:50.259 --> 00:50:51.704
Hi.

542
00:50:57.766 --> 00:51:01.772
- Wow. This should be in a museum.
- Oh, it's nothing.

543
00:51:01.872 --> 00:51:05.960
Just quail egg and asparagus in filo pastry
with a cream of rocket sauce.

544
00:51:06.876 --> 00:51:09.340
Well, my regular is baked beans.

545
00:51:10.881 --> 00:51:14.315
Good old British baked bean.
Zero nutritional value.

546
00:51:14.850 --> 00:51:17.251
Yeah. But good on toast.

547
00:51:18.588 --> 00:51:20.522
Oh, you know I can't drink.

548
00:51:20.622 --> 00:51:24.859
Of course. But how are we going to cope
without the numbing haze of alcohol?

549
00:51:26.462 --> 00:51:30.431
Why can't you drink?
If that's not a rude question?

550
00:51:33.602 --> 00:51:35.271
Alex?

551
00:51:37.539 --> 00:51:38.969
What?

552
00:51:49.019 --> 00:51:50.854
Didn't... Didn't...

553
00:51:50.954 --> 00:51:53.187
Alex and I are pregnant.

554
00:51:53.622 --> 00:51:56.115
Twelve and a half weeks in.

555
00:51:59.561 --> 00:52:01.495
That's wonderful.

556
00:52:02.699 --> 00:52:06.233
Congratulations. Congratulations.

557
00:52:07.303 --> 00:52:11.708
- Alex, you didn't tell me?
- No, I... Sorry, I thought I did.

558
00:52:12.108 --> 00:52:13.774
That's...

559
00:52:15.310 --> 00:52:17.481
Let me help! Shit!

560
00:52:17.581 --> 00:52:19.246
Daddy's antique table! Alex, quick!

561
00:52:19.982 --> 00:52:21.719
- Oh, bollocks.
- Language, please!

562
00:52:22.119 --> 00:52:25.686
- Oh, fuck!
- No! Why can't you just say fudge?

563
00:52:40.502 --> 00:52:43.079
Look what you made me do.

564
00:52:45.608 --> 00:52:48.512
It's fine. It's okay.

565
00:52:48.612 --> 00:52:52.516
We have Herb's vernissage
in an hour... It's...

566
00:52:52.616 --> 00:52:55.282
Everything is gonna be fine.

567
00:53:11.967 --> 00:53:14.134
I'm so sorry.

568
00:53:15.071 --> 00:53:18.842
Sally had this planned for weeks.
It's not for long, okay? I promise.

569
00:53:18.942 --> 00:53:22.045
Sweetie? Dr. Jones is by the
sweet and sour prawn balls!

570
00:53:22.145 --> 00:53:24.915
- He's just...
- Sweetie, not now. Okay?

571
00:53:25.015 --> 00:53:28.151
But he's a senior
thoracic surgeon, Alex.

572
00:53:28.251 --> 00:53:30.953
She's right, Alex. Go on.

573
00:53:31.053 --> 00:53:32.866
Okay, let's go. Let's go.

574
00:53:35.391 --> 00:53:38.929
This image here is one of my favorites.

575
00:53:39.029 --> 00:53:41.727
How to articulate that transient moment

576
00:53:41.827 --> 00:53:46.802
when you see something
through the camera's eye.

577
00:53:46.902 --> 00:53:51.275
It's a little like love at first sight.
Stops you in your tracks.

578
00:53:51.375 --> 00:53:55.278
Suddenly you recognize it
for exactly what it is.

579
00:53:55.378 --> 00:53:57.135
A load of bollocks.

580
00:54:02.686 --> 00:54:06.256
- Rosie! Rosie, where are you going?
- Back home.

581
00:54:06.356 --> 00:54:08.058
And I mean England.
This is too crazy for me, okay?

582
00:54:08.158 --> 00:54:10.060
I walked straight into the middle
of something here!

583
00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:14.598
Look, it's all fine, honestly.
Sally and I just needed to air some stuff!

584
00:54:14.698 --> 00:54:16.564
Oh, good, I'm glad you're fine,
'cause I'm not!

585
00:54:17.399 --> 00:54:19.569
We were out together
the whole night, Alex!

586
00:54:19.669 --> 00:54:23.689
And all the while your girlfriend was at home
expecting a baby! And you didn't say!

587
00:54:23.789 --> 00:54:27.044
Come on, Rosie. Nothing happened,
we were just... We were just having some fun.

588
00:54:27.144 --> 00:54:30.113
That's what you got me
over here for then? Just some fun?

589
00:54:30.213 --> 00:54:33.250
I wanted to see you!
For Christ sake, you're my best friend!

590
00:54:33.350 --> 00:54:37.985
Or maybe you needed someone
from your old life to point out the truth!

591
00:54:40.522 --> 00:54:42.826
- What truth?
- You're in a mess, Alex!

592
00:54:42.926 --> 00:54:46.096
This whole situation
is one big bloody giant mess!

593
00:54:46.196 --> 00:54:47.364
Me? I'm in a mess?

594
00:54:47.464 --> 00:54:49.873
- And you're in denial!
- You're projecting!

595
00:54:49.973 --> 00:54:52.369
Okay, can we just stop
the psychobabble here

596
00:54:52.469 --> 00:54:54.704
and just talk like
English people, please!

597
00:54:54.804 --> 00:54:57.041
Fine! Fine! Fine. Fine. Look.

598
00:54:57.341 --> 00:55:01.445
I was worried you might find it hard,
you know, coming here.

599
00:55:01.745 --> 00:55:05.378
- Hard?
- I mean, you've had a tough time, Rosie, and...

600
00:55:05.814 --> 00:55:10.319
seeing where we live, you know,
our apartment, our lifestyle, it's just...

601
00:55:10.494 --> 00:55:13.657
You thought I was jealous of you? No.

602
00:55:13.757 --> 00:55:15.548
I pity you, Alex!

603
00:55:16.162 --> 00:55:19.229
All I see is someone compensating
for a crap personal life

604
00:55:19.329 --> 00:55:22.433
- by schmoozing his way up the career ladder!
- Crap personal life?

605
00:55:22.633 --> 00:55:26.268
All right, let's see. Stable relationship
with beautiful girlfriend,

606
00:55:26.368 --> 00:55:29.287
lots in common, a great circle
of friends, a kid on the way,

607
00:55:29.387 --> 00:55:31.500
who's gonna have two parents,
by the way, not one!

608
00:55:40.816 --> 00:55:43.650
- Rosie, come on, I...
- Forget it, Alex!

609
00:55:44.353 --> 00:55:48.024
- Go ahead and climb your greasy pole!
- You know, I will!

610
00:55:48.224 --> 00:55:51.161
Just don't come whinging to me
when you realize you're empty inside.

611
00:55:51.261 --> 00:55:53.160
- No danger of that!
- Good!

612
00:55:53.896 --> 00:55:56.613
- Excellent!
- Fantastic!

613
00:56:18.102 --> 00:56:20.531
<i>In a little while from now</i>

614
00:56:20.631 --> 00:56:23.232
<i>If I'm not feeling any less sour</i>

615
00:56:23.332 --> 00:56:28.873
<i>I promised myself to treat myself
and visit a nearby tower</i>

616
00:56:28.973 --> 00:56:31.605
<i>And climbing to the top</i>

617
00:56:31.705 --> 00:56:34.393
<i>Will throw myself off</i>

618
00:56:34.493 --> 00:56:37.242
<i>In an effort to make it clear to who</i>

619
00:56:37.342 --> 00:56:39.806
<i>Ever what it's like when your shattered</i>

620
00:56:39.906 --> 00:56:42.372
<i>Left standing in the lurch</i>

621
00:56:42.472 --> 00:56:45.525
<i>At a church where people're saying</i>

622
00:56:45.625 --> 00:56:48.283
<i>"My God that's tough, she stood him up!</i>

623
00:56:48.383 --> 00:56:51.401
<i>No point in us remaining.</i>

624
00:56:51.501 --> 00:56:53.931
<i>May as well go home."</i>

625
00:56:54.031 --> 00:56:56.703
<i>As I did on my own</i>

626
00:56:56.803 --> 00:57:00.967
<i>Alone again, naturally</i>

627
00:57:02.319 --> 00:57:07.046
<i>It seems to me that there are
more hearts broken in the world</i>

628
00:57:07.146 --> 00:57:12.631
<i>That can't be mended, left unattended</i>

629
00:57:12.731 --> 00:57:15.080
<i>What do we do?</i>

630
00:57:15.530 --> 00:57:17.901
<i>What do we do?</i>

631
00:57:24.692 --> 00:57:27.432
<i>Alone again</i>

632
00:57:27.532 --> 00:57:29.908
<i>Naturally</i>

633
00:57:42.404 --> 00:57:43.941
Oh, no!

634
00:57:44.973 --> 00:57:46.440
Pleased to see me?

635
00:57:47.042 --> 00:57:48.111
What are you doing here?

636
00:57:48.211 --> 00:57:50.781
You sent me Katie's drawing!
I got on the first flight I could!

637
00:57:51.181 --> 00:57:54.117
No! No, no, no!
I did that on a whim, okay?

638
00:57:54.217 --> 00:57:57.420
Katie drew the picture, and it was a mistake!
I never expected you to actually show up!

639
00:57:57.520 --> 00:58:01.657
That letter really made me think about my life!
I wanna meet her, Rosie! I am her dad.

640
00:58:02.257 --> 00:58:03.802
Dad?

641
00:58:04.293 --> 00:58:07.328
And what precisely is it that you think
qualifies you for that title? Those?

642
00:58:08.364 --> 00:58:12.002
Where were you, "Dad" when she woke up with
colic every night for the first few months?

643
00:58:12.102 --> 00:58:15.771
Or cut her first tooth,
or took her first steps?

644
00:58:16.173 --> 00:58:18.672
Has anyone ever told you,
you have the most amazing eyes?

645
00:58:26.448 --> 00:58:30.687
Look, I'm sorry, okay? I get it,
I bailed on you. I was a total creep.

646
00:58:30.787 --> 00:58:32.822
But there hasn't been a single day
in the last five years

647
00:58:32.922 --> 00:58:34.691
that I haven't wondered what she's like.

648
00:58:34.791 --> 00:58:38.027
Is she like me?
Did she luck out on the gene front?

649
00:58:38.127 --> 00:58:39.709
You're so full of shit!

650
00:58:46.101 --> 00:58:49.973
You have to give me a chance, Rosie!
I can be different, I promise.

651
00:58:50.373 --> 00:58:53.243
Do you want me to crawl on my hands and knees?
Anything, Rosie! I'm begging you!

652
00:58:53.343 --> 00:58:56.913
Get up, you idiot. If this were about me,
I'd be driving you to the airport right now!

653
00:58:57.013 --> 00:58:59.215
You'd be right to.

654
00:59:01.583 --> 00:59:03.602
One chance!

655
00:59:04.687 --> 00:59:06.823
One chance,
but any mess-ups and you're out.

656
00:59:07.023 --> 00:59:09.927
And you be nice! And I don't
just mean average nice, I mean,

657
00:59:10.027 --> 00:59:12.896
Father Christmas-Easter
Bunny-Tom-Hanks-all-rolled-into-one nice!

658
00:59:12.996 --> 00:59:14.698
- Yeah.
- And you will buy her...

659
00:59:14.898 --> 00:59:17.896
the most expensive pair of
shitty pink shoes that you can find!

660
00:59:19.768 --> 00:59:21.935
I'm gonna Google them right now.

661
00:59:33.548 --> 00:59:34.719
- Hi-five!
- Boo!

662
01:00:09.985 --> 01:00:11.919
Wait a minute. You did what?

663
01:00:13.621 --> 01:00:18.127
Hey! This is a man who let you
go to casualty on your own

664
01:00:18.227 --> 01:00:21.064
in the middle of the night,
with a condom stuck up your fanny!

665
01:00:21.164 --> 01:00:23.300
He's Katie's dad.

666
01:00:23.400 --> 01:00:26.002
You should see her little face
light up when he walks in the room!

667
01:00:26.102 --> 01:00:28.118
They're really bonding.

668
01:00:29.171 --> 01:00:32.042
Of course, none of that would matter
if he had a crap bod.

669
01:00:32.142 --> 01:00:34.641
He's really worked on that thing. Wow.

670
01:00:35.377 --> 01:00:37.107
You're evil, Rosie Dunne.

671
01:00:39.181 --> 01:00:41.818
I just want to belong to someone, Ruby.

672
01:00:41.918 --> 01:00:44.351
I'm tired of waiting.

673
01:00:44.453 --> 01:00:46.987
And it feels good with him.

674
01:00:47.656 --> 01:00:49.423
We're a family.

675
01:01:20.790 --> 01:01:24.127
- Can you just stop jumping up and down?
- I'm just checking everyone's here.

676
01:01:24.227 --> 01:01:26.829
Everyone being who, exactly?

677
01:01:26.929 --> 01:01:29.832
- How's the blushing bride?
- Like a mad bunny.

678
01:01:29.932 --> 01:01:32.398
Okay. Okay.

679
01:01:36.171 --> 01:01:39.376
Don't take this
the wrong way, love. But...

680
01:01:39.476 --> 01:01:44.547
if there's any part of you that
isn't sure, even now, say the word.

681
01:01:44.647 --> 01:01:46.780
We'll walk straight out of here,
our heads held high.

682
01:01:47.783 --> 01:01:49.049
So you like Greg, then?

683
01:01:50.385 --> 01:01:52.753
Come on. Let's get you hitched.

684
01:03:09.998 --> 01:03:11.188
Do you like this?

685
01:03:11.500 --> 01:03:14.667
- Katie, would you please?
- Mom!

686
01:03:15.871 --> 01:03:17.636
Sorry.

687
01:03:36.091 --> 01:03:38.160
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Sally...

688
01:03:38.260 --> 01:03:39.794
Rosie.

689
01:03:41.196 --> 01:03:44.532
- What can I do for you?
- Is Alex there?

690
01:03:44.832 --> 01:03:46.168
Did he not tell you?

691
01:03:46.268 --> 01:03:48.905
- <i>Tell me what?</i>
- Alex and I separated.

692
01:03:49.005 --> 01:03:51.975
- What? When?
- <i>About eight weeks ago?</i>

693
01:03:52.075 --> 01:03:54.571
Pretty much the day of your wedding.

694
01:03:59.147 --> 01:04:02.082
- Oh, God!
- <i>What?</i>

695
01:04:02.951 --> 01:04:05.788
- <i>What?</i>
- I think my water just broke!

696
01:04:05.888 --> 01:04:09.058
Oh, God! Wait, wait. Are you sure?
Maybe you just wet yourself.

697
01:04:09.158 --> 01:04:11.494
No, I did not wet myself! Where is Herb?

698
01:04:11.594 --> 01:04:12.995
- <i>Herb?</i>
- Oh, God.

699
01:04:13.095 --> 01:04:15.461
<i>- Who, the artist?</i>
- Herb!

700
01:04:15.830 --> 01:04:17.884
It's happening! The baby!

701
01:04:18.533 --> 01:04:22.397
It's coming! Herb!

702
01:05:42.951 --> 01:05:44.184
Katie!

703
01:05:48.323 --> 01:05:51.127
- Mom! You're supposed to knock!
- The music! It's too loud!

704
01:05:51.227 --> 01:05:53.793
Can't hear you! The music's too loud!

705
01:05:54.763 --> 01:05:58.084
- Don't do that!
- Yeah, this music needs to be felt.

706
01:05:59.401 --> 01:06:01.437
Is that lipstick you're wearing?

707
01:06:01.537 --> 01:06:04.304
Privacy, Mom! Please!

708
01:06:05.040 --> 01:06:06.599
Okay!

709
01:06:08.311 --> 01:06:09.912
Now, have you got the thermal
underwear I gave you?

710
01:06:10.012 --> 01:06:13.014
- It's the Mediterranean.
- What about cash?

711
01:06:13.114 --> 01:06:16.631
I've got some extra if you like.
Phone chargers? Your wallet, Dad?

712
01:06:16.731 --> 01:06:19.087
Rosie, it's fine. Will you stop
fussing like a mother hen?

713
01:06:19.387 --> 01:06:20.523
Yes.

714
01:06:20.723 --> 01:06:22.091
- Goodbye!
- Love you.

715
01:06:22.191 --> 01:06:23.159
- Get in.
- Love you.

716
01:06:23.359 --> 01:06:24.492
- Bye!
- Bye!

717
01:06:25.092 --> 01:06:27.126
- Bye.
- Bye.

718
01:06:29.198 --> 01:06:31.300
<i>So my parents have sold up
and gone backpacking,</i>

719
01:06:31.400 --> 01:06:34.771
<i>while I get to stay to stay at home
nagging a 12-year-old about lipstick.</i>

720
01:06:34.971 --> 01:06:39.005
I mean, seriously, could you find
further proof of how fucked up my life is?

721
01:06:42.710 --> 01:06:43.711
Bethany?

722
01:06:43.811 --> 01:06:46.773
Rosie Dunne! You work here now?

723
01:06:47.949 --> 01:06:50.018
I just got promoted to reception.

724
01:06:50.618 --> 01:06:52.455
Congratulations!

725
01:06:52.555 --> 01:06:55.291
But you! Your success,
it's... It's amazing!

726
01:06:55.991 --> 01:06:58.594
I've just flown from Morocco,
tomorrow I fly out again,

727
01:06:58.694 --> 01:07:00.897
New York, Boston, Chicago, nightmare.

728
01:07:00.997 --> 01:07:03.132
- The heart bleeds.
- Yeah.

729
01:07:03.232 --> 01:07:05.766
Boston? You should look up Alex.

730
01:07:05.866 --> 01:07:09.672
Really? Alex Stewart?
You guys still keep in touch?

731
01:07:09.872 --> 01:07:12.775
Of course. He could do
with a friendly face.

732
01:07:12.875 --> 01:07:15.583
Great! I'll get his details
from you later!

733
01:07:15.877 --> 01:07:17.408
Thanks.

734
01:07:17.508 --> 01:07:21.045
Could I have some Evian sent up to my room?
It's the only water I can drink.

735
01:07:21.145 --> 01:07:24.951
Three bottles.
And maid service twice a day?

736
01:07:25.620 --> 01:07:27.353
Of course.

737
01:07:30.592 --> 01:07:32.559
That's how fucked-up your life is.

738
01:07:44.205 --> 01:07:45.244
Mom!

739
01:07:45.444 --> 01:07:48.908
How is Nice? Have you found
some good places to eat?

740
01:07:53.949 --> 01:07:56.082
Mom, are you all right?

741
01:07:57.485 --> 01:07:59.311
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

742
01:08:00.021 --> 01:08:01.454
<i>I'm...</i>

743
01:08:05.093 --> 01:08:06.960
Mom, what is it?

744
01:08:08.296 --> 01:08:10.491
<i>It's bad news for you.</i>

745
01:08:11.191 --> 01:08:12.599
Mom?

746
01:08:13.835 --> 01:08:15.969
Mom, what is it?

747
01:09:13.594 --> 01:09:14.512
Hey.

748
01:09:16.164 --> 01:09:17.532
Really?

749
01:09:18.232 --> 01:09:19.843
Yeah.

750
01:09:25.774 --> 01:09:27.951
When I heard,

751
01:09:28.711 --> 01:09:31.746
the years fell away, I was...

752
01:09:31.846 --> 01:09:34.114
I was a fucked-up kid all over again.

753
01:09:36.518 --> 01:09:39.752
Hero worshipping
this amazing dad you had.

754
01:09:54.369 --> 01:09:56.144
Sorry.

755
01:10:01.909 --> 01:10:04.073
I never got to say goodbye.

756
01:10:04.412 --> 01:10:07.814
Hey, come here. Come here, you. Hey.

757
01:10:15.923 --> 01:10:19.104
Hey, hey! Hands off my woman!

758
01:10:22.931 --> 01:10:26.799
I've just been chatting to your cousin.
She is such a bore.

759
01:10:28.636 --> 01:10:31.904
Seriously? Are you pissed?

760
01:10:33.908 --> 01:10:36.245
I find funerals really difficult, Alex.

761
01:10:36.345 --> 01:10:39.048
'cause Rosie, I mean,
she's having a great time.

762
01:10:39.248 --> 01:10:42.520
- You know what? Fuck you!
- Please.

763
01:10:43.785 --> 01:10:47.357
Thanks for turning up.
We both really appreciate your support.

764
01:10:47.822 --> 01:10:49.656
Let's go, come on.

765
01:11:02.737 --> 01:11:04.370
<i>Rosie,</i>

766
01:11:05.207 --> 01:11:09.212
<i>you deserve someone who loves you
with every beat of his heart,</i>

767
01:11:09.612 --> 01:11:13.947
<i>someone who'll always be there for you,
and who'll love every part of you...</i>

768
01:11:39.007 --> 01:11:41.243
Mom! I'm not going
without my grey skinny jeans!

769
01:11:41.343 --> 01:11:43.510
All right! I'll get them for you!

770
01:12:02.230 --> 01:12:05.367
- "Rosie, you deserve someone who..."
- Anything for me?

771
01:12:05.902 --> 01:12:08.801
Yeah, just this one.

772
01:12:12.375 --> 01:12:14.155
From Dad.

773
01:12:14.555 --> 01:12:17.792
- In France, the day before he died.
- Oh, God, don't read that.

774
01:12:17.892 --> 01:12:20.513
- What?
- Well, it'll upset you.

775
01:12:22.149 --> 01:12:23.883
I'm already upset.

776
01:12:24.919 --> 01:12:25.985
Right.

777
01:12:28.389 --> 01:12:30.481
Do you want me to stay?

778
01:12:32.427 --> 01:12:34.293
Funnily enough, no.

779
01:12:35.063 --> 01:12:38.097
Okay. Well, call me if you
need anything, okay?

780
01:12:51.079 --> 01:12:54.447
<i>Dear Rosie, I can't believe it.</i>

781
01:12:54.783 --> 01:13:00.052
<i>Here I am at last, finally walking
the Mediterranean coast.</i>

782
01:13:00.956 --> 01:13:04.527
<i>I've lost count of the years
I've waited for this moment.</i>

783
01:13:04.627 --> 01:13:06.996
<i>Somehow life got in the way.</i>

784
01:13:07.096 --> 01:13:10.331
<i>And it was all good,
I don't regret a minute of it,</i>

785
01:13:10.431 --> 01:13:13.499
<i>but we forget our dreams at our peril.</i>

786
01:13:13.868 --> 01:13:18.875
<i>I know you had yours, too, and it must feel
sometimes like they're gone for good.</i>

787
01:13:18.975 --> 01:13:23.042
<i>But I'm so proud of the woman
you've become, Rosie,</i>

788
01:13:23.344 --> 01:13:25.945
<i>of the mother you've been to Katie.</i>

789
01:13:26.481 --> 01:13:29.233
<i>What I once said
about you is still true,</i>

790
01:13:29.333 --> 01:13:33.422
<i>there's nothing you can't do
if you put your mind to it.</i>

791
01:13:33.522 --> 01:13:37.325
<i>So keep chasing those dreams,
will you, darling?</i>

792
01:13:37.425 --> 01:13:39.286
<i>For my sake,</i>

793
01:13:39.642 --> 01:13:41.386
<i>Dad.</i>

794
01:13:52.307 --> 01:13:56.309
How can someone
just not be there anymore?

795
01:14:00.114 --> 01:14:01.247
Fuck knows.

796
01:14:06.888 --> 01:14:11.725
At least he did everything he wanted.
He didn't forget his dreams.

797
01:14:17.264 --> 01:14:19.765
What if I told you

798
01:14:19.867 --> 01:14:22.701
I was gonna use my share

799
01:14:23.004 --> 01:14:27.640
of the money from the house
and get myself a hotel?

800
01:14:28.309 --> 01:14:30.676
Somewhere simple but...

801
01:14:31.112 --> 01:14:33.379
But my own place.

802
01:14:34.315 --> 01:14:37.149
I think that would be awesome, Mom.

803
01:14:44.359 --> 01:14:48.696
<i>Rosie, I understand that you
haven't been in touch. And...</i>

804
01:14:48.796 --> 01:14:50.893
<i>I just need to know one thing.</i>

805
01:14:53.100 --> 01:14:55.229
<i>Are you happy with him?</i>

806
01:14:58.740 --> 01:15:02.344
<i>There's not much I got right
in my life, but this family,</i>

807
01:15:02.444 --> 01:15:04.781
<i>somehow we're making it work.</i>

808
01:15:04.881 --> 01:15:08.363
<i>So I guess the one word answer
to your question should be,</i>

809
01:15:09.116 --> 01:15:10.683
<i>"Yes."</i>

810
01:15:18.593 --> 01:15:20.162
- Hey!
- Hi.

811
01:15:20.262 --> 01:15:22.465
So look at this. The Sweetlands Hotel.

812
01:15:22.565 --> 01:15:24.611
That's where we had our
end of school dance!

813
01:15:24.711 --> 01:15:27.770
They just joined our group. I mean,
I was just checking for discounts,

814
01:15:27.870 --> 01:15:30.369
and I found this booking...

815
01:15:31.305 --> 01:15:35.811
That's Greg's name!
The bridal suite, for this weekend!

816
01:15:35.911 --> 01:15:38.314
He's already up there on business.

817
01:15:38.414 --> 01:15:42.285
Do you think... For our anniversary?

818
01:15:45.286 --> 01:15:46.896
It's him.

819
01:15:50.124 --> 01:15:51.293
Hey!

820
01:15:51.393 --> 01:15:55.864
<i>Hey, gorgeous. Listen, I'm gonna
have to stay here a few extra nights,</i>

821
01:15:55.964 --> 01:15:58.700
<i>the guys need me to check out
some more venues.</i>

822
01:15:58.800 --> 01:16:00.391
<i>Can you take Katie and go to your mom's,</i>

823
01:16:00.491 --> 01:16:03.336
<i>and then I can swing by
on Sunday and pick you up?</i>

824
01:16:04.772 --> 01:16:06.270
<i>Babe?</i>

825
01:16:07.274 --> 01:16:08.808
Fine.

826
01:16:09.010 --> 01:16:11.176
<i>Cool, see you later, then.</i>

827
01:16:11.412 --> 01:16:13.646
- Talk later.
<i>- Bye.</i>

828
01:16:17.118 --> 01:16:19.160
Check the booking.

829
01:16:22.690 --> 01:16:25.088
Here it is. Bridal suite for two,

830
01:16:25.188 --> 01:16:28.093
checked in two hours ago.

831
01:16:29.396 --> 01:16:31.364
Oh, Rosie, I'm...

832
01:16:51.048 --> 01:16:53.419
Rosie? What are you going to say?

833
01:17:03.030 --> 01:17:04.463
Fuck!

834
01:18:07.895 --> 01:18:09.513
"Rosie,

835
01:18:09.932 --> 01:18:13.435
"you deserve someone who loves you
with every beat of his heart.

836
01:18:13.535 --> 01:18:15.905
"Someone who will always
be there for you,

837
01:18:16.005 --> 01:18:19.107
"and who will love every part of you,
especially your flaws.

838
01:18:19.207 --> 01:18:23.753
<i>"I know Katie needs her dad. I don't
want to intrude. So if this is all wrong,</i>

839
01:18:23.853 --> 01:18:26.912
<i>"just ignore it and I promise
I'll never broach the subject again.</i>

840
01:18:28.015 --> 01:18:30.650
<i>"Greg's not the man for you, Rosie.</i>

841
01:18:30.985 --> 01:18:33.225
<i>"Twice I've let you
slip through my fingers.</i>

842
01:18:33.325 --> 01:18:36.091
<i>"Let's stop being afraid
and take the chance.</i>

843
01:18:36.191 --> 01:18:40.042
<i>"I know now I can make you happy.
Call me if you feel the same way.</i>

844
01:18:41.128 --> 01:18:42.862
<i>"Love, Alex."</i>

845
01:19:28.075 --> 01:19:29.463
Bethany?

846
01:19:30.244 --> 01:19:33.379
- What are you doing there?
- <i>I live here now. I moved in.</i>

847
01:19:34.982 --> 01:19:38.385
- <i>Look who it is, Mr. Schnuffs!</i>
- Mr. Schnuffs?

848
01:19:38.685 --> 01:19:40.319
<i>Rosie?</i>

849
01:19:49.561 --> 01:19:51.800
<i>Baby, that thing we were
talking about earlier.</i>

850
01:19:51.900 --> 01:19:53.769
<i>- Yeah.
- Ask her now.</i>

851
01:19:53.869 --> 01:19:55.380
<i>Schnuffie...</i>

852
01:19:59.840 --> 01:20:01.707
<i>Bethany and me,</i>

853
01:20:02.849 --> 01:20:05.180
<i>We thought, why hang around, you know,</i>

854
01:20:05.280 --> 01:20:08.615
<i>So, she started organizing
the whole thing,</i>

855
01:20:08.715 --> 01:20:12.485
<i>but then Phil said no,
so your name came up, obviously.</i>

856
01:20:14.155 --> 01:20:15.921
<i>We're getting married!</i>

857
01:20:16.992 --> 01:20:19.694
<i>The wedding's next week.
It's fast, but we need to fit it in</i>

858
01:20:19.794 --> 01:20:23.832
<i>before New York Fashion Week.
And you have to be our best man!</i>

859
01:20:23.932 --> 01:20:25.835
<i>I mean, you are a girl but... Right?</i>

860
01:20:25.935 --> 01:20:28.704
<i>This is all because of you, Rosie.
You told me to come here.</i>

861
01:20:28.804 --> 01:20:32.204
<i>It wouldn't have happened if
it wasn't for you. Thank you.</i>

862
01:20:36.210 --> 01:20:38.680
It is so great having you as a friend.

863
01:20:38.780 --> 01:20:41.383
I mean, every time something goes wrong
in my life, all I got to do is look at yours

864
01:20:41.483 --> 01:20:43.901
and it puts everything into perspective.

865
01:20:44.051 --> 01:20:46.541
He proposed to her on a boat.

866
01:20:46.641 --> 01:20:50.292
It's like... It's like Kate and Leonardo
in that scene on the deck.

867
01:20:50.392 --> 01:20:52.344
The <i>Titanic.</i>

868
01:20:53.127 --> 01:20:55.178
How appropriate. Look,

869
01:20:55.278 --> 01:20:58.700
Alex is yours, he always has been.
This is just proof of ownership.

870
01:20:58.800 --> 01:21:01.202
He wrote that months ago!

871
01:21:01.302 --> 01:21:04.337
- And anyway he's my best friend!
- No!

872
01:21:05.105 --> 01:21:07.840
I'm your best friend! Get it yet?

873
01:21:08.843 --> 01:21:10.476
We just keep missing each other.

874
01:21:12.279 --> 01:21:13.982
Maybe we're just not meant to be.

875
01:21:14.982 --> 01:21:17.811
Right. Let me just try and explain this
in a language you might understand.

876
01:21:19.054 --> 01:21:22.591
Ship. Iceberg. Ship hits iceberg.

877
01:21:22.691 --> 01:21:26.161
Mayhem, horror, ocean of ice

878
01:21:26.261 --> 01:21:29.064
and then Alex on the last lifeboat.

879
01:21:29.364 --> 01:21:31.248
One space left. Is it Bethany?

880
01:21:32.633 --> 01:21:34.615
Or Rosie?

881
01:21:35.636 --> 01:21:37.839
Who's it going to be?

882
01:21:41.054 --> 01:21:42.444
What? You're immigrating now?

883
01:21:42.544 --> 01:21:45.410
Less time, more outfits.
You're paying excess.

884
01:21:45.510 --> 01:21:46.583
What is this? A school outing?

885
01:21:46.683 --> 01:21:49.718
I couldn't leave her behind
and wherever Katie goes, Toby goes.

886
01:21:49.818 --> 01:21:51.887
Oh, are you two an item now?

887
01:21:51.987 --> 01:21:53.622
- No way. We're friends.
- No way. We're friends.

888
01:21:53.722 --> 01:21:56.178
God give me strength.
Well, come on, we're really late.

889
01:21:56.278 --> 01:21:58.594
Relax. I hate arriving early,

890
01:21:58.694 --> 01:22:01.227
and besides, we have a five or six
hour cushion on the other side.

891
01:22:09.169 --> 01:22:10.939
- Sorry, what's going on?
- Volcanic ash.

892
01:22:11.039 --> 01:22:12.340
I need to go to Boston!

893
01:22:12.440 --> 01:22:15.743
I'm afraid it's a five to six hour delay.
Sir, I understand...

894
01:22:15.843 --> 01:22:17.610
I think your cushion just burst.

895
01:22:26.621 --> 01:22:28.990
Slow down! I'm not wearing a sports bra!

896
01:22:29.190 --> 01:22:31.293
Okay, you guys, get your stuff!

897
01:22:31.393 --> 01:22:33.962
- Katie move it!
- I'm coming, I'm coming!

898
01:22:34.062 --> 01:22:37.062
- Ruby, come on!
- Mom!

899
01:22:40.067 --> 01:22:43.150
And you thought the flight was rough.
You'll have to get dressed in the van!

900
01:22:43.250 --> 01:22:46.738
We are so late!

901
01:22:51.546 --> 01:22:53.982
- Excuse me?
- You get everything the wrong way round over here.

902
01:22:54.082 --> 01:22:55.684
- And you are?
- Ruby.

903
01:22:55.784 --> 01:22:57.919
- A pleasure to meet you, Ruby.
- Likewise.

904
01:22:58.019 --> 01:23:00.935
- Will you marry me?
- Yeah.

905
01:23:01.121 --> 01:23:03.676
What? That's not...
That's not fair! That's not...

906
01:23:03.776 --> 01:23:06.091
It can't be that easy, it's not...

907
01:23:17.238 --> 01:23:19.541
I think she wants all the women
around her to look fat.

908
01:23:19.641 --> 01:23:21.574
Well, it works.

909
01:23:35.690 --> 01:23:38.724
No, no, you don't know how hard it is.

910
01:24:00.280 --> 01:24:04.987
Final word of warning. Alex can hold
his drink to an almost lethal degree,

911
01:24:05.087 --> 01:24:06.743
as I discovered on my 18th birthday,

912
01:24:06.843 --> 01:24:10.225
when he decided a night of
tequila slammers was the way to go.

913
01:24:12.327 --> 01:24:14.830
Well, you know when people say
that they were so drunk,

914
01:24:14.930 --> 01:24:19.000
that the whole night is a blank and you
always go, "No way, not possible."

915
01:24:19.100 --> 01:24:23.001
Well, believe me, it's possible.

916
01:24:34.081 --> 01:24:36.163
Choosing a...

917
01:24:36.263 --> 01:24:40.252
Choosing the person that you
want to share your life with

918
01:24:40.988 --> 01:24:44.333
is one of the most important decisions

919
01:24:44.433 --> 01:24:46.625
any of us makes,

920
01:24:47.127 --> 01:24:48.692
ever.

921
01:24:50.164 --> 01:24:55.033
Because when it's wrong,
it turns your life to grey.

922
01:24:55.169 --> 01:24:59.841
And sometimes...
sometimes you don't even notice

923
01:24:59.941 --> 01:25:04.843
until you wake up one morning
and realize years have gone by.

924
01:25:06.113 --> 01:25:08.059
We both know about that one, Alex.

925
01:25:10.718 --> 01:25:13.217
Your friendship has brought

926
01:25:13.317 --> 01:25:16.041
glorious Technicolor to my life.

927
01:25:16.323 --> 01:25:19.393
It's been there even
in the darkest of times.

928
01:25:19.493 --> 01:25:23.128
And I am the luckiest
person alive for that gift.

929
01:25:25.332 --> 01:25:27.266
I hope I didn't take it for granted.

930
01:25:28.202 --> 01:25:32.874
I think maybe I did.
Because sometimes you don't see

931
01:25:32.974 --> 01:25:36.608
that the best thing that's ever
happened to you is sitting there,

932
01:25:36.708 --> 01:25:38.880
right under your nose.

933
01:25:39.913 --> 01:25:42.380
But that's fine, too.

934
01:25:42.883 --> 01:25:44.860
It really is.

935
01:25:45.185 --> 01:25:47.835
Because I've realized that...

936
01:25:49.389 --> 01:25:51.856
no matter where you are

937
01:25:52.659 --> 01:25:56.694
or what you're doing,
or who you're with,

938
01:25:57.831 --> 01:26:00.347
I will always

939
01:26:01.034 --> 01:26:03.067
honestly,

940
01:26:03.167 --> 01:26:06.860
truly, completely

941
01:26:06.960 --> 01:26:08.754
love you.

942
01:26:24.725 --> 01:26:29.329
Like a sister loves a brother

943
01:26:29.429 --> 01:26:32.164
and a friend loves a friend.

944
01:26:33.767 --> 01:26:37.269
I'll always stand guard
over your dreams, Alex.

945
01:26:37.504 --> 01:26:41.940
No matter how weird or twisted they get.

946
01:26:46.413 --> 01:26:49.483
So, please, everybody,

947
01:26:49.583 --> 01:26:51.586
join me in a toast.

948
01:26:51.686 --> 01:26:54.617
To the bride and groom.

949
01:26:55.222 --> 01:26:58.056
To the bride and groom!

950
01:27:07.568 --> 01:27:11.873
- Come on, show me what you've got!
- No, please! Well, okay then! Ready?

951
01:27:11.973 --> 01:27:14.406
Here we go. You like it?

952
01:27:53.981 --> 01:27:56.714
Baby, what's up?

953
01:28:03.023 --> 01:28:04.802
Katie?

954
01:28:06.760 --> 01:28:08.827
- Katie just...
- She just went through here.

955
01:28:09.663 --> 01:28:11.548
Katie?

956
01:28:11.648 --> 01:28:13.432
Mom?

957
01:28:14.602 --> 01:28:16.943
What are you doing out here?

